# Intent: Train 2 item 7, the hourly chime and its quiet-hours rule (features.md Always-on). One soft tone (the shipped "ready" sound) at the top of each hour, off until a person turns it on with self.audio.hourly_chime (saved in the unit's own namespace mp_daily). Rules, all in a plain-C core: never without a set clock, never twice in one hour, never in quiet hours (the person's window from set_sound_policy, or 22:00 to 07:00 when none is set) or while the host says it is dark, never while the unit speaks, listens or rings a timer (it tries again while the minute lasts), and always through the sound policy and the hard mute. It ignores "sounds at night are fine": a chime is not something a person must notice. A `chime` event tells the host it sounded. The tool's test flag decides now as if it were the top of an hour. Rides the T01 one-second tick: no task, no timer. The quiet-hours rule is new code beside the 115 policy core (it reads that policy; it does not change it).
# Placement: unit (the chime must sound with the host off; the host only reads the event)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_sounds.cc of the StackChan main component (MIT)
# Check after a flash: self.audio.hourly_chime enabled=1 test=true answers result=chime and one success tone, or result=quiet in quiet hours; with sounds off or the unit muted the tone is refused by the policy and no tone sounds. Left on, a chime sounds at the next top of the hour outside quiet hours.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_HOURLY_CHIME (default y); off removes the chime and the tool.
